      "title": "Separating the Variables in a Differential Equation"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "d8947f89-5f67-5c6c-a047-bbbf469ddeb6",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{x+2}\n$$\n\nWork on a domain where all displayed expressions are defined.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A differential equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differential equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(\\frac{x}{x+2})\\cdot {y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{x+2}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "c01492cc-1df0-5058-9563-5e9a8957d705",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
